      "name": null,
      "problem": "Evaluate $P(7,4).$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\,.\n$$\n\n$P(7,4)$ means the same thing as ${}_{7}{P}_{4}.$ Using the usual formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(7,4) & =\\frac{7!}{(7-4)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7!}{3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4\\cdot \\cancel{3!}}{\\cancel{3!}} \\\\  & =840.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
